        "heading": "",
        "intro": "",
        "html": "<p>We&#39;d rather you spend less and buy right. Here&#39;s our honest list. It includes things we don&#39;t sell.</p>\n<h2>Worth it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Two pairs of gloves:</strong> a good match pair and a tougher training pair. Nothing extends the life of your match gloves more.</li>\n<li><strong>Glove wash, used after every session.</strong> Dirt and sweat kill latex faster than saves do.</li>\n<li><strong>Padded shorts, if you play on anything harder than soft grass.</strong> Hips first.</li>\n<li><strong>Finger tape,</strong> if you&#39;ve jarred fingers before. It&#39;s cheap and it works.</li>\n<li><strong>Grip socks,</strong> if your feet move inside your boots when you push off.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Usually not worth it</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Top-range match gloves for training on turf.</strong> Rubber crumb can wear through expensive soft latex in weeks.</li>\n<li><strong>Fingersaves &quot;just in case&quot;.</strong> They&#39;re useful after an injury, but for many keepers they cost feel.</li>\n<li><strong>Buying gloves a size up to grow into.</strong> A loose glove costs you catches.</li>\n<li><strong>Care &quot;systems&quot; with five bottles.</strong> Wash, grip spray and a deodorizer cover it.</li>\n<li><strong>Anything sold with a permanent &quot;was&quot; price.</strong> If it&#39;s always 40% off, it was never that price.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Where we fit in</h2>\n<p>We make the things on the &quot;worth it&quot; list that you buy again and again: glove care, tape and socks. We price them to be bought monthly, not once. Where we can&#39;t beat what already exists, we&#39;ll say so.</p>",
        "narrow": true,
        "tone": "ink",
